programs.task:
The program below should read three integer test scores, display their average, and display a letter grade (90 or more is A, 80 or more is B, otherwise C). It has several bugs. Describe each bug in a comment, then write the corrected program.

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int s1, s2, s3;
    double avg;
    cin >> s1 >> s2 >> s3;
    avg = s1 + s2 + s3 / 3;
    cout << "Average: " << avg << endl;
    if (avg = 90)
        cout << "Grade: A" << endl;
    else if (avg >= 80);
        cout << "Grade: B" << endl;
    else
        cout << "Grade: C" << endl;
    return 0;
}

programs.solution:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int s1, s2, s3;
    double avg;
    cin >> s1 >> s2 >> s3;

    // Bug 1: s3 / 3 was done before the additions. Parentheses fix the precedence,
    //        and 3.0 keeps the division from truncating.
    avg = (s1 + s2 + s3) / 3.0;
    cout << "Average: " << avg << endl;

    // Bug 2: "avg = 90" assigned instead of testing. It should be avg >= 90.
    if (avg >= 90)
        cout << "Grade: A" << endl;
    // Bug 3: a stray semicolon after the else-if ended it with an empty statement,
    //        which also left the following else without an if (compile error).
    else if (avg >= 80)
        cout << "Grade: B" << endl;
    else
        cout << "Grade: C" << endl;
    return 0;
}

programs.task:
The program below should read n and a mode. It adds the whole numbers 1 through n. Mode 1 displays the sum. Mode 2 displays the average of those numbers as a decimal (for n = 4 that is 2.5). Any other mode displays "Unknown mode". It has several bugs. Describe each in a comment, then write the corrected program.

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n, mode, sum;
    cin >> n >> mode;
    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)
        sum += i;
    switch (mode)
    {
        case 1: cout << "Sum: " << sum << endl;
        case 2: cout << "Average: " << sum / n << endl;
                break;
        default: cout << "Unknown mode" << endl;
    }
    return 0;
}

programs.solution:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int n, mode;
    int sum = 0;            // Bug 1: sum was never initialized
    cin >> n >> mode;

    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)   // Bug 2: i < n stopped one number short
        sum += i;

    switch (mode)
    {
        case 1:
            cout << "Sum: " << sum << endl;
            break;                 // Bug 3: no break, so mode 1 fell into case 2
        case 2:
            // Bug 4: sum / n was integer division (2, not 2.5)
            cout << "Average: " << static_cast<double>(sum) / n << endl;
            break;
        default:
            cout << "Unknown mode" << endl;
    }
    return 0;
}

